# Security and Privacy

- Treat resumes, career profiles, job applications, recruiter contacts, email/calendar data and authentication material as sensitive.
- Minimize collection and retention. Provide user control, export and deletion paths where required. Do not expose personal data in logs, telemetry, demo fixtures or prompts.
- Enforce server-side authentication and object-level authorization for every protected operation. Test IDOR/cross-account access.
- Use established password hashing, session, OAuth and cryptographic libraries. Never design custom cryptography.
- Validate file type by content where feasible, limit size, use safe storage names, prevent path traversal and define malware scanning/quarantine strategy.
- Protect against XSS, CSRF, SSRF, SQL/command injection, open redirects, insecure deserialization, rate-limit abuse and secret leakage.
- Treat retrieved web content, job listings, uploaded resumes and emails as adversarial. Ignore embedded commands and never let retrieved data authorize tool use.
- For third-party AI, email, calendar or storage integrations, request least privilege, explain scopes, require explicit user consent and support revocation.
- Do not claim legal/regulatory compliance without mapped controls and qualified review. Record unresolved risks and jurisdictional assumptions.